-- title:
--   A face with a unique parent lies on a cube boundary
-- statement:
--   Work in an $n$-dimensional cubical Sperner grid $\{0,\ldots,p\}^n$. A simplex is an injective ordered list of vertices, nondecreasing in every coordinate, whose first and last vertices differ by at most one in each coordinate.
--
--   If an ordered list $I$ has exactly one parent $n$-simplex, then some coordinate is constantly $0$ or some coordinate is constantly $p$:
--
--   $$I\text{ has a unique parent}\Rightarrow I\subseteq\{x_k=0\}\text{ or }I\subseteq\{x_k=p\}\text{ for some }k.$$
--
--   This relates the combinatorial boundary definition to the geometric cube boundary.
-- source:
--   https://prove2.me/submissions/facf5b05-d302-42c1-a107-8ff40a0c2134; boundary_is_A_or_B, lines 3121-3138

